course: dictionary
lesson: 11604
title: Applicable and applies
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Applicable is a formal word. It means relevant, or able to be used in a particular case. If something is applicable, it applies to you or to this situation. «Tick the box if applicable» means: only tick it if it applies to you.
explain: Look at the words around it. On a form you might read, «Question 7: Do you have a pet? Tick the box if applicable.» If you have no pet, the question does not apply to you, so you leave the box empty. The clues tell you that applicable and applies belong to the same family.
explain: In maths, a rule can be applicable to all numbers, or only to some. «This rule is applicable only to even numbers» tells you the rule works for 2, 4, 6 and so on, but not for 3 or 5. Try your meaning in the sentence: "this rule applies only to even numbers" still makes sense, so you know you are right.
fact: Applicable means relevant, or able to be used in a particular case.
fact: «Applicable» comes from the word «applies», which means it is connected to something.
fact: «Not applicable (N/A)» means the question does not apply to you or to this case.
fact: «Tick the box if applicable» means tick it only if it fits your situation.
fact: Everyday words that mean the same thing are «relevant» and «that applies», but applicable is more formal and is used on forms and in rules.
exercise: «Tick the box if applicable.» What does applicable mean here? | Ignore the box completely | Tick every box, always | *Only if it applies to you | Put a cross in the box
exercise: On a form, Ravi sees «Not applicable (N/A)» next to the question about his pet. What does it mean? | The question is about his pet | *The question does not apply to him | The question is very difficult | He must answer it twice
exercise: «The rule is applicable only to even numbers.» Which numbers does the rule apply to? | Odd numbers | Only the number 1 | All numbers, always | *Even numbers
test:
Mia reads, «Tick if applicable: I have a bike.» What does applicable mean in this sentence? | Easy to read | *Relevant, or true for her | Very large | Hidden
test:
Which word means about the same as applicable in «This rule is applicable here»? | Forgotten | Broken | *Relevant | Far away
exam:
A teacher writes, «This rule is applicable to fractions only, not to whole numbers.» Which numbers does the rule apply to? | Whole numbers | *Fractions | Both fractions and whole numbers | Neither, the rule is never used
